A||||1||Austin||O2 Sensor Prob.||||4||
Z||000000||Austin||11-13-2001||04:04 PM||||I have an O2 sensor problem on my 86 S.E.  I need to know where it is located and how to change the sucker.  Any pics of the engine bay showing where it is would be helpful.  ||||reg||4
Z||000001||JohnF||11-13-2001||04:33 PM||||Easy to see and find!  For V6, look in the exhaust pipe just as it goes vertical at the firewall for a sensor about 2" long sticking out of the side of the pipe.  It has about a 15" piece of single strand wire that runs from it to wiring harness.<P>Same as for 4 banger, just located in pipe on aft side of engine.<P>See Haynes pp. 6-5.<P>Unscrew it using an open-end wrench, screw in another and hook it up.  Disconnect battery (I've heard) to reset ECM after sensor change.||||reg||1
